  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the formal assembly scene as the perpetrator of historical atrocities",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the visual material of the formal assembly (scene_1) and the textual material ('we destroy the world and kill a lot of people.'), which collectively represent the Nazi Party leadership and members. The text uses 'we' to directly attribute the actions of destruction and mass killing to the group depicted in the image. This creates a semiotic projection where the viewer (user) is positioned as part of or identified with the collective entity shown, thereby internalizing the historical responsibility implied by the text. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the first-person plural 'we' in the text creates a direct projection of the user onto the historical actors depicted.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
